1
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,670
- Hi everyone. And welcome.

2
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:09,740
So today we have a hamstring ball workout.

3
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:13,290
We're going to target the glutes,
hamstrings, abs, and core.

4
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:14,940
The timer is going to be on throughout,

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:18,100
45 seconds of work, 15 second rest.

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,870
Some exercises will be
performed for four sets,

7
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:22,230
others, two sets.

8
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,650
Simply follow along.

9
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:25,690
Stability balls come in various sizes.

10
00:00:25,690 --> 00:00:28,577
And also depending on how
hard it is actually pumped up,

11
00:00:28,577 --> 00:00:30,080
make this your own workout,

12
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,220
place your foot position
where is comfortable for you.

13
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:34,930
When you're doing the
hamstring ball roll outs,

14
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:37,570
as you can see here, try to control it.

15
00:00:37,570 --> 00:00:40,090
Keep the hips up as high
as you can throughout.

16
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:41,010
Some of the exercises

17
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:45,120
you will also see me stabilising
with my elbows on the mat.

18
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,160
Others, I will lift my arms up

19
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:49,290
to make it that little
bit more challenging.

20
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:51,190
So of course it is your preference.

21
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:52,040
Play about.

22
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,000
This is not easy.

23
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:53,833
And especially

24
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:55,650
if you're not used to
stability ball workouts,

25
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:57,260
this is intense.

26
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:59,550
If you've never tried a
stability ball workout,

27
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:00,670
or you even go to the gym

28
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:02,150
and there is that
stability ball lying there

29
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:03,340
and you don't know what to do with it,

30
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,860
give this workout a go.

31
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:07,540
Your hamstrings will
be completely on fire.

32
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:08,480
Hamstring ball roll outs

33
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:11,570
have always been one of my
favourite hamstring exercises,

34
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:13,650
although it has been such a
long time since I've done it,

35
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,850
so I'm really looking
forward to doing this today.

36
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:18,260
Stability balls are always
a really good option

37
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:21,080
to have at home if you're
training from home.

38
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,470
And come in further videos,

39
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:25,650
I do expect to use the
stability ball a lot more.

40
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:28,420
Try not to get too frustrated
if you are new to this.

41
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:29,480
Take it slow.

42
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:32,470
You will progress quite quickly
if you keep practising .

43
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:34,750
We'll kick it off with the
hamstrings, moving on to abs,

44
00:01:34,750 --> 00:01:37,560
and then we have a little
finisher back on those hamstrings.

45
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,393
Let's go.

